iams  and what followed at the scene the metro  police department  then made policy changes the board  includes four commissioned officers  and three citizens from a pool of 20  which  donovan britt david skelton and richard  metzler  are part of i would say the majority of  our cases that i've served on this year  haven't even haven't  involved the use of a gun it's been  other issues where the  the person died going hands-on what's  important to  myself and probably every member of the  board is transparency  it's what we look for there has to be  someone on that bridge that people can  trust and say look  i was in that room this is what i saw i  was on the scene i spoke to the chief we  spoke as a group together  and i'm telling you this is how this  case went now at the same time there  also has to be that that notion that we  can be critical  and supportive at the same time  tonight at 11 we'll take a closer look  at the in-custody death of byron  williams and we'll also take a look  at the number of use of force incidents  reporting live vanessa murphy 8 news now

